    <output type="code">src/client/pcf/TrackingFieldTrio/index.ts</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the lifted `TrackingFieldTrio` in `@spaarke/ui-components`, when grepped, then it uses no React-18/19-only runtime API (`createRoot`/`use(`/Actions) and no `as React.ComponentType` cast — it renders under both React 16/17 and React 19 (NFR-05).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the shared core, when inspected, then it contains no `sprk_communication`-specific access-permission integers/labels — all options + field labels are injected via props (entity-agnostic, FR-14).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the lifted component with injected values + onChange, when monitor/high-priority/access-permission are changed, then each fires onChange with the correct value (read/write identical to the PCF).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the `TrackingFieldTrio` PCF, when built with `npm run build:prod`, then it compiles clean importing the component from `@spaarke/ui-components`, injecting its `sprk_communication` options + labels, its local duplicate deleted, and its standard-control `ReactDOM.render` lifecycle + read/write behavior unchanged (regression-free, NFR-04).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a dark `FluentProvider` theme, when the component renders, then all three flags + injected segment colors are legible (ADR-021 dark mode).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the `@spaarke/ui-components` barrel, when imported, then it re-exports `TrackingFieldTrio` + its option types (available to task 035's reader-pane view); no business logic duplicated between PCF and shared lib.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Shared lib build + PCF `build:prod` both green; existing `TrackingFieldTrio` unit tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Cite spec FR-18 + FR-14 + NFR-04 + NFR-05 + ADR-021 in the PR. EXTRACTION/lift of existing code (COMPLETE-class) — no §11 `&lt;justification&gt;` (modify/refactor exempt). Targets `@spaarke/ui-components` (generic), a DIFFERENT barrel from 021/022 — no P2 barrel contention. Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `@spaarke/ui-components`). Completion summary appended here when done.</notes>

